      "content": "I hear you, but honestly, the Board is already hyper-focused on cost-cutting this quarter. If we lead with a 25% spike in Engineering, they're going to start questioning our retention strategies and potentially looking into headcount reductions there. \n\nIt feels like a bit of an outlier compared to the rest of the company. Can we rephrase this to be more about the general stability of the tech org? Maybe frame the turnover as part of the usual seasonal movement or talent upgrading? I just don't want to create a fire where there isn't one.",
